  "description": "A pending stale-grid choice is durable, so it survives a second restart (5.52; C6 decision 3). On a declared gap the core forces a snapshot, and the commit, the grid_snapshot_record and stale_seq are ONE bbolt write, so a core that dies after writing one asks for what follows the loss and declares no loss twice, and the prompt survives. A grid that cannot be rebuilt though no byte was lost (snapshot_incompatible or seq_jump) is found at restore, before any new commit, so its stale_seq/stale_cause write stands alone and precedes the first new commit. stale_seq is where staleness began for both causes; stale_cause is gap or grid_lost. Both are present or neither, as the v0.2 ends_at/ends_by/ending trio is written; cleared on the answer. Refused: one without the other, and a cause the vocabulary does not hold.",
